Convert a .slint file to XML, HTML, an Apple Storyboard or GTK Blueprint

Usage: slint-convert[EXE] [OPTIONS] --to <TO> <INPUT>

Arguments:
  <INPUT>  The .slint file to convert

Options:
      --to <TO>              Output format [possible values: xml, html, storyboard, blueprint]
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>      Write here instead of standard output
      --platform <PLATFORM>  Storyboard framework [default: uikit] [possible values: uikit, appkit]
      --strict               Treat every warning as an error
  -h, --help                 Print help
  -V, --version              Print version
